sequenceDiagram
    participant User as Trader
    participant CD as CyberDeltaEngine
    participant ML as ML Module
    participant FRS as Funding Rate Strategy
    participant BP as Backpack API (CEX)
    participant HL as Hyperliquid API (DEX)
    participant PX as Paradex API (DEX)
    participant RM as Risk Management

    Note over CD,RM: Initialization Phase
    User->>CD: Initialize trading bot (Funding Rate Strategy)
    CD->>FRS: Initialize funding rate parameters
    CD->>RM: Set dynamic risk limits (VaR_t = f(σ_mkt), CVaR, max position)
    CD->>ML: Activate ML for E[FR] prediction

    Note over CD,PX: Data Collection Phase
    loop Collect Market Data
        par Fetch CEX Data
            CD->>BP: Fetch perp prices, funding rates, oracle data
            BP-->>CD: Backpack Market Data (Validated)
        and Fetch DEX Data (Hyperliquid)
            CD->>HL: Fetch perp prices, funding rates, oracle/mark data
            HL-->>CD: Hyperliquid Market Data (Validated)
        and Fetch DEX Data (Paradex)
            CD->>PX: Fetch perp prices, funding rates, oracle/mark data
            PX-->>CD: Paradex Market Data (Validated)
        end
        CD->>CD: Reconcile data discrepancies
    end

    Note over CD,RM: Analysis Phase
    CD->>FRS: Process funding rate data (BP, HL, PX)
    FRS->>ML: Predict E[FR] = μ_FR + ε
    FRS->>FRS: Calculate basis volatility (σ_B,t) per exchange/pair
    FRS->>FRS: Compute no-arbitrage bounds with E[FR]
    FRS->>FRS: Calculate NFD_adj = NFD_raw - (Txn_Costs + Slippage)
    FRS-->>CD: Enhanced funding arbitrage signals

    CD->>RM: Calculate Kelly sizing with ML signals
    RM->>RM: Apply fractional Kelly (e.g., 0.5f*)
    RM->>RM: Check risk constraints (√w^T Σw <= MaxRisk_t)
    RM-->>CD: Optimized position sizing

    Note over CD,User: Decision & Execution Phase
    CD->>CD: Rank opportunities by U = E[Return] / (σ_Return * Risk_Tolerance)
    alt Single-Exchange Funding Arbitrage (e.g., HL)
        CD->>HL: Execute delta-neutral position (Latency-adjusted)
        Note over CD,HL: Capturing HL funding rate
    else Cross-Exchange Arbitrage (e.g., BP vs HL)
        CD->>BP: Execute Leg 1 (Short Perp, t_exec modeled)
        CD->>HL: Execute Leg 2 (Long Perp, t_exec modeled)
        Note over CD,HL: Exploiting BP vs HL differential
    end
    CD->>RM: Monitor positions with real-time risk metrics

    Note over CD,User: Monitoring & Adaptation
    loop Every funding period
        par Collect Funding
            CD->>BP: Check/Receive funding payments
            BP-->>CD: Funding settlement info
            CD->>HL: Check/Receive funding payments
            HL-->>CD: Funding settlement info
            CD->>PX: Check/Receive funding payments
            PX-->>CD: Funding settlement info
        end
        CD->>CD: Update PnL and E[Returns]
    end

    loop Real-Time Adaptation
        CD->>FRS: Update σ_B,t and NFD_adj
        FRS-->>CD: Refreshed estimates
        CD->>RM: Adjust positions (ΔPosition = K_p * Error + ...)
        CD->>ML: Refine E[FR] with feedback
    end

    CD->>User: Enhanced metrics (PnL, Sharpe Ratio, Risk Exposure)